   "commit": "60ca342",
   "date": "2026-11-25",
   "what": "this version (tag open-camready-20261125): names, comments, messages and documents changed. The guard of 2026-11-24 is the option guard: harness/option_guard.py, tested by tests/test_option_guard.py (debug options are not allowed in benchmark proofs); its functions, constants and log file (logs/option_guard.log), the field it writes on a replaced record and the fast stage's intermediate input file (input.option-guard.jsonl) are named after it, and the files that import it follow. The post ops' site check (harness/post/opus_screen.py, opus_stepdrop.py and the ops that use the shared check) skips any proof that sets a debug option (was: one option name). One redundant text rule of the guard removed: every set_option debug.* form is still rejected, and the Arena's forbidden list, which runs first, rejects the meta-programming commands. The --target default of post_fast/pf_drive.py and post_fast/snapshot.py is 81.4367, the tier C file's stored mean (it only sets the summary's time-to-target). Tests: names and texts edited, two tests of tests/test_option_guard.py dropped, tests/test_axiom_guard.py checks this version's fingerprint. The seven post-stage scripts' fingerprint is b4ac6d42002767a0 (seven_post_scripts). Tier B measured again on this code: stored mean 81.4665 in 85 min, 57 rows changed, 0 fell (measured.tierB_20261125)",
